---
import BaseHead from '../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title="Tokenizer Ablation | Ravikumar Buragapu"
			description="A from-scratch byte-level BPE tokenizer and controlled downstream code-identifier ablation at fixed token and byte budgets."
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<p>RESEARCH PROTOTYPE · TOKENIZATION · CONTROLLED ABLATION</p>
			<h1>Tokenizer Ablation</h1>
			<p>
				How much does tokenizer choice change what a small model
				learns? This experiment trains a byte-level BPE tokenizer
				from scratch, sweeps its vocabulary size, and measures
				code-identifier classification accuracy with the same
				fixed-width classifier at fixed token and byte budgets.
			</p>

			<section aria-labelledby="experiment">
				<h2 id="experiment">Measure the tokenizer, not a moving target</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>Pure-Python byte-level BPE training with byte fallback.</li>
					<li>Vocabulary sweep: 1k, 4k, 16k, and 32k.</li>
					<li>Eight-class code-identifier classification task.</li>
					<li>Compare accuracy and classifier fit time at fixed token and UTF-8 byte budgets.</li>
					<li>Optional tiktoken cl100k_base and Hugging Face BERT WordPiece references.</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					The corpus and task are generated and intentionally
					limited. The results are not claims about pretrained
					LLMs, arithmetic, or language-model quality.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="demo">
				<h2 id="demo">Run the experiment</h2>
				<pre><code>cd tokenizer-ablation
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e ".[dev]"
tokenizer-ablation --output results/ablation.json
pytest</code></pre>
				<p>
					<a href="https://github.com/buragapuravi/my_research_work/tree/main/tokenizer-ablation"
						>Read the project README</a
					>
					·
					<a href="/projects/learned-ann">Explore Learned ANN Index</a>
				</p>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
